{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the minimum order for a hoodie style with multiple colors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The 300-piece MOQ applies per style, and can typically be split across 3-4 colors and a full size range within that single style minimum — you don't need 300 pieces of one exact color."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you print or embroider on fleece without distorting the fabric?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, with the right method for the fabric weight. Puff print and embroidery both work well on brushed fleece and French terry above 260gsm; on lighter fleece we recommend a stabilizer backing for embroidery to prevent puckering."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the difference between brushed fleece and French terry for my brand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Brushed fleece is warmer and has a more traditional hoodie feel at a lower cost — good for basics and high-volume programs. French terry is lighter, drapes better, and reads as a more premium product — common for streetwear and elevated basics lines willing to pay a moderate premium per piece."}},
